title: $:/config/cypro/Sections
type: application/x-tiddler-dictionary

<!--
  Sections config — the data-driven sidebar (Phase 3, task 137 step 3.4).

  The sidebar (macros? $:/plugins/aeckert/cypro/sidebar) renders one block per
  "<n>-caption" index; each section lists PAGES by slug ("1-pages"). For every
  slug `pg`:
    `pg`            = the navigated tiddler title
    `pg-caption`    = German display label used while the data tiddler does not
                      exist yet (first run) — the data tiddler's own `caption`
                      field always wins.
  The green/red light per item shows whether ALL checks whose `page` field
  points at that tiddler evaluate as passed. Adding a page or a check therefore
  means touching this tiddler (or nothing at all for checks' fields drive state).

  NOTE: never hard-code page titles in the sidebar — everything comes from here.
-->
1-caption: Grundsätzliches
1-pages: company contactPerson BSIPortal
2-caption: Risikomanagement
2-pages: identificationKIKS listKIKS identificationRisk monitoring drr
3-caption: Personalangelegenheiten
3-pages: backgroundcheck training

company: $:/cypro/data/company
company-caption: Unternehmensdaten
